  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(169.83pt, 117.55pt, " offer complementary perspectives on the same data. When creating a ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 132.3pt, "data-based model, various sources of information are collected to achieve high association ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 147.05pt, "with the target (represented by red pixels in the pairwise matrix). However, each interaction ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 161.55pt, "may not provide unique information for prediction. ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(346.4pt, 161.55pt, "MKAN")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(377.65pt, 161.55pt, " finds simple interactions that ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 176.3pt, "dominate prediction based on specific inputs. This approach differs from typical machine ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 190.8pt, "learning, which often weights all associations (without regularization) to achieve optimal ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 205.58pt, "performance. ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 226.33pt, "KAN-based analysis can therefore support feature prioritization in high-dimensional spaces, ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 240.83pt, "as demonstrated through the CAMELS attribute optimization experiment. Beyond ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 255.58pt, "simplification and enhanced interpretability, pruning improves computational efficiency, ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 270.08pt, "making it valuable in large-scale or resource-limited modeling. Accordingly, ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(460.7pt, 270.08pt, "KAN ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(485.2pt, 270.08pt, "matrices ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 284.85pt, "as preprocessing tools guide scientists towards simpler, and more transparent data-based ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 299.6pt, "representations. Further, as with the Computational Fluid Dynamics experiment, KAN ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 314.1pt, "matrices can facilitate diagnostic post-processing analyses in complex systems where ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 328.85pt, "governing mechanisms are often unclear, improving understanding. ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 349.35pt, "Finally, dual characterization of association strength and functional form is critical for ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 364.12pt, "understanding any data-generating process. The ability to robustly estimate relational form ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 378.62pt, "and strength from data, while providing insights into the direction and structure of ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 393.37pt, "information flow, is a common scientific challenge that extends well beyond hydrology and ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 408.12pt, "fluid dynamics. Moreover, knowledge of functional form can help to expose hidden ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 422.62pt, "knowledge, while providing consistency checks against existing domain knowledge. For ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 437.4pt, "these reasons, KAN matrix analysis shows strong potential for improving interpretability in ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 452.15pt, "machine learning and deepening scientific understanding across diverse domains. ")
