  #line-at(286.13pt, 93.03pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(294.13pt, 97.03pt, ". They consider the ratio between the standard ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 111.53pt, "deviation of edge activation results and the standard deviation of the connected node. This ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 126.3pt, "ratio defines the edge’s contribution to the node. However, it does not account for the ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 141.05pt, "entire network. Therefore, they compute the ratio iteratively, moving from the output layer ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 155.55pt, "to the input layer, counting the effective connectivity of edges before and after a specific ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 170.3pt, "edge. This method provides a more accurate estimation of feature contribution than the ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 185.05pt, "original L1 norm used by ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#4472c4"))
  #line-at(207.58pt, 185.05pt, "Liu et al.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(248.85pt, 181.05pt, "19")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(256.85pt, 185.05pt, ". ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 205.58pt, "In this paper, the ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#4472c4"))
  #line-at(170.58pt, 205.58pt, "Liu et al.")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 8pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#0000ff"))
  #line-at(211.6pt, 201.58pt, "20")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.35pt, 205.58pt, " attribute score is normalized to ensure scores on the range 0-1 ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 220.33pt, "for plotting in the KAN matrix. However, that does not consider the predictive strength of ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 234.83pt, "the resulting associations. To address this, the attribute score is multiplied by a ")
  #line-at(85.025pt, 249.58pt, "performance metric that characterizes predictive strength. Two metrics were tested: the ")
  #set text(font: "Calibri", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
